Used here: the 14 emotions' keyframes (src/duckmind/neuro/emotions_data.json, rounded from keyframes/*.json and
emotions.json), the sound designs and timings (re-made in each duck's own voice: src/duckmind/simweb/emotion_voice.py,
a port of quack.py and of the workshop's sounds/make_*.py recipes at tag workshop-2026-10-07), and the way the official
runtime plays them (robot/pad-expressions.patch, read only: head targets are deltas from HOME on robot.head, body pitch
on robot.pose, the beak on robot.mouth).

Also used (2026-10-11, play dead lies down): the two scripted joint poses of play dead (emotions.json ``pose_joints``) and the
workshop's ``robot.poseJoints`` / per-servo torque-off (patch 19 of robot/pad-expressions.patch, ported to the simulator's
robotd 0.15.0 build: third_party/microduck_emotions/robotd-poseJoints.patch, built by build-robotd-pose-joints.sh; simulator only).

Changes: the sounds are made with the simulated duck's voice seed, not the robot's; the keyframes are played by the
neural duck's body link (neuro/emotions.py) under its safety rules. Copy of the licence: ./LICENSE.
Full source (with the patch, previews and the workshop tag): the upstream repository above, at the same commit.
